  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nA feed of moisture from off the Great Lakes has allowed scattered to \nbroken cloud cover and a few light showers to persist this \nafternoon. However, high pressure building in from the west should \nbring an end to any lingering precipitation by evening. Breezy \nconditions will also diminish by the end of the day.\n\nFor tonight, temperatures are expected to dive into the 20s to 30s \nunder clearing skies and calm to light flow. Therefore, a Freeze \nWarning is effect for the entire forecast area late tonight through \nearly Sunday morning. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nWhile a low pressure system meanders up along the East Coast next \nweek, the Middle Ohio Valley is expected to remain dry with high \npressure in control through the end of the work week. Although \ndaytime temperatures should be right around normal for this time of \nyear, the early mornings remain chilly through mid week. If the \ngrowing season is not ended by tonight's freeze, then additional \nfrost/freeze products may be warranted late Sunday night into early \nMonday morning.",
